 dway to Alcatraz Avenue. Start at Halloween Hub\nPrice: Free\nCategories: 
 community\, free\nSource: funcheap/south-bay+funcheap/east-bay\n\nCelebrat
 e Halloween at the 34th Annual Rockridge Halloween Parade \, a free\, fami
 ly-friendly tradition featuring trick-or-treating\, crafts\, face painting
 \, costume contests for kids and pups\, and festive activities at more tha
 n 40 participating locations along College Avenue\, from Broadway to Alcat
 raz Avenue. Start at Halloween Hub #1 in the Rockridge Library parking lot
  (5366 College Ave.) for crafts hosted by the Museum of Children’s Art (
 MOCHA)\, free commemorative trick-or-treat bags while supplies last\, and 
 entertainment featuring the Ricky Roo and Friends puppet show at 11 a.m.\,
  musician Asheba at noon\, and librarian storytime at 1 p.m. Halloween Hub
  #2 at College Avenue Presbyterian Church (5951 College Ave.) offers famil
 y crafts\, a photo booth and additional entertainment. Throughout the dist
 rict\, over 40 participating businesses will offer Halloween treats\, acti
 vities and surprises. Come in costume\, bring the kids and four-legged fam
 ily members\, and enjoy a spirited afternoon supporting Rockridge’s loca
 lly owned shops and restaurants. Rockridge Halloween Parade Sunday\, Octob
 er 25\, 2026 | 11a-2p Rockridge District\, 5366 College Ave\, Oakland FREE
  – All ages Getting there: The e
